  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\nThe central idea is to solve the Erd\u0151s overlap problem using a combination of **symmetric function construction**, **gradient-based optimization**, and **population-based search**. The rationale is that step functions in the overlap minimization problem often exhibit symmetry, especially with respect to rotations and translations. By enforcing symmetry, we can reduce the effective search space while still discovering high-quality solutions. The optimization algorithm is designed to:\n\n- Escape local optima by maintaining multiple symmetric representations of candidate solutions\n- Use projected gradients to enforce constraints efficiently\n- Adjust the waveform complexity (pulse width vs height) to find lower overlap values\n\nThis differs from the provided strategy by avoiding:\n1. Differential evolution (too slow for high resolutions)\n2. Random restarts (inefficient for constrained optimization)\n3. Full matrix correlation computes (too expensive)\n\nThe primary limitation is that the triangle wave with real-valued parameters may not capture the optimal symmetry, but higher resolutions could fix this. Key limitations include the parameterization by continuous variables, which might limit pulse strength, but randomization in amplitudes may overcome this.\n\n2. Mathematical specifications\n\nVariables: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = \u1e46\nObjective: C\u2085 = argmax\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \u2248 max\u2096 (neighbors_overlap(h, k)) * dx\nConstraints: \u2211h[i] * dx = 1 (with dx=2/n), h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\nRepresentation: Pulse-based with segments of positive/negative values\nObjective surrogate: Smoothened overlap at geometric shifts\nFeasibility guarantee: Projection and scaling ensure solution validity\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n\n1. Input: seed, budget_s, initial_h_values\n2. Set n=280, dx=2/n, integral_target=n/2\n3. Precompute neighbors_overlap() by convolution\n4. Initialize population of wave-like candidates:\n   - Create initial waveform (symmetric triangle with random parameters)\n   - Constrain by projection and scaling\n   Maintain diversity by randomization\n5. Each GA cycle:\n   a. Sample new candidate by mutation:\n      - Deformation pulse structure\n      - Random jitter in amplitudes\n   b. Project to [0,1] and adjust integral\n   c. Score using max-shifted correlation\n   d. Update best candidate\n   e. Score and compare\n6. GA termination: \n   - Time budget exceeded (100s total)\n   - Stable improvement (smaller grad norm)\n7. Local refinement: GD to local minima with projected gradient\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n\nBase configuration:\n- Simple triangle wave\n- Pulse width tuning range: [0.3, 0.7]\n- Element count: 145 pulses\n- Fit attempts: 4-parameter minimization\n- Sample factor: n\u2080=32, then project to 280\n\nVariants (conditional execution):\n- Reduced_pulse: Fewer pulses for speed\n- High_amp: Higher variance amplitudes\n- Variable_step: Random step changes per cycle\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n\n- DE tradeoff: Early GA exit if no improvement\n- Budget split: 80s GA, 20s refinement\n- Param sweep: 1 minute/variant, skip uncovered\n- Integral adjustment: Feathering projection\n- Time thresholds: Live updates per candidate cycle\n- Fallback: Parent if constraint violated\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n\nEach candidate must satisfy:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- |\u2211h[i]*dx - 1| < 0.005\n- Catch NaNs in correlation\n- Return best_c5 score\n\nFinal validation sample score every 5 cycles\nObjective consistency check: Cross-verify max overlap",
